  "summary_en": "European Commission communication setting the Data Union Strategy to improve data access for AI. It proposes data labs, scaled common European data spaces, a Digital Omnibus simplifying data and GDPR rules, one-click compliance, and an international data policy against localisation. Robotics and autonomous driving appear only in passing.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Launch data labs within AI Factories to pool, curate and pseudonymise data for AI training",
   "Digital Omnibus to repeal the Data Governance Act and Free Flow Regulation and merge them into the Data Act",
   "Targeted GDPR amendments clarifying legitimate interest for AI training and anonymisation criteria",
   "Guidance, standards and voluntary certification for synthetic data, and a European data quality standard",
   "Anti-data-leakage toolbox and guidelines on third-country treatment of EU data (2026)"
  ],
